<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_core-5-missing-information-message-exchange" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Camunda Modeler" exporterVersion="5.51.0" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.9.0">
  <bpmn:error id="Error_INVALID_VARIABLE" name="INVALID_VARIABLE" errorCode="INVALID_VARIABLE" />
  <bpmn:message id="Message_MissingInformationSupplied" name="missing-information-supplied">
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <zeebe:subscription correlationKey="=referralId" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
  </bpmn:message>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_1">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Hospital" name="Hospital Trust" processRef="core-5-missing-information-message-exchange" />
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Referring" name="Referring GP or another hospital" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="MessageFlow_M1" name="missing information request" sourceRef="N_MS_RequestDocuments" targetRef="Participant_Referring" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="MessageFlow_M2" name="missing information supplied" sourceRef="Participant_Referring" targetRef="N_MS_DocumentsSupplied" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="core-5-missing-information-message-exchange" name="Core 5 - Missing information requested from, and supplied by, the referring organisation" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Covers FR-003 with BR-01, BR-02 and EX-01: the Medical Secretaries check a referral for the supporting information it is expected to carry, record what is missing and ask the referring organisation for it, and they do not assess the patient's clinical suitability. The request leaves the pool as the message missing-information-requested, published by the request-referral-documents worker and correlated by referralId; the process then waits on an intermediate message catch event for missing-information-supplied, so the answer arrives when the referring organisation sends it rather than being assumed. The reply itself is published by the participant that supplies the documents - a message flow into this pool is not something this process can send. A request the worker refuses returns to the task that owns it, which is where the request was recorded, so it is corrected and sent again (FR-003, NFR-008). The reply is recorded against the request it answers before the documents are checked, so what was asked for, when, and whether it has arrived is a hospital record rather than something only the instance knows (FR-003, NFR-008).</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_1">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_MedicalSecretaries" name="Medical Secretaries">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_ReferralReceived</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_MergeMissingItems</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_RecordMissingItems</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_DocumentsSupplied</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_RecordReceipt</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_CheckSuppliedDocuments</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_DocumentsComplete</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_ReadyForReview</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>N_MS_RequestDocuments</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>B_MS_ReceiptInvalid</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>B_MS_RequestInvalid</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="N_MS_ReferralReceived" name="Referral received with information missing">
      <bpmn:documentation>The referral has arrived and its supporting information is incomplete (BR-01, EX-01).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="N_MS_MergeMissingItems" name="Request recorded, still incomplete or refused">
      <bpmn:documentation>Merges the paths that reach Record the missing information (Referral received with information missing, Are the documents complete now?, request unusable, receipt unusable). The merge is exclusive - each token that arrives continues on its own - and it is drawn rather than left implicit at the activity. The first request, a request made again because the reply was still incomplete and one the worker refused all come back to the task that owns the request (BR-01, EX-01, NFR-008).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:userTask id="N_MS_RecordMissingItems" name="Record the missing information">
      <bpmn:documentation>Supplies the request-referral-documents inputs referralId, requestedFrom and requestedItems: which referral is missing documentation, who has to be asked for it and what is missing. referralId is also the value the reply is correlated by. This task owns the request, so an unusable one returns here to be corrected and sent again rather than the instance stalling on an incident (BR-02, FR-003, NFR-008).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:userTask />
        <zeebe:formDefinition formId="missing-information-request" />
        <zeebe:assignmentDefinition candidateGroups="medical-secretaries" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent id="N_MS_DocumentsSupplied" name="Missing information received">
      <bpmn:documentation>The reply is waited for rather than assumed: the subscription is correlated by referralId, so it is this referral's answer that moves this instance on and not another patient's (FR-003, EX-01, NFR-004).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MessageEventDefinition_Supplied" messageRef="Message_MissingInformationSupplied" />
    </bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="N_MS_RecordReceipt" name="Record the supplied documents">
      <bpmn:documentation>Job type record-document-receipt (worker document-receipt; marks the information request recorded when it was sent as supplied). Input: referralId. Output: informationRequestStatus, documentsReceivedDate. Error: INVALID_VARIABLE (FR-003, EX-01, NFR-008).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="record-document-receipt" retries="3" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="N_MS_CheckSuppliedDocuments" name="Check the supplied documents">
      <bpmn:documentation>The same documentation checklist is applied to what has now arrived: it reads the referral against the expected supporting information and records whether anything is still outstanding. documentsComplete decides whether the referring organisation is asked again (BR-01, FR-003).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:userTask />
        <zeebe:formDefinition formId="referral-check" />
        <zeebe:assignmentDefinition candidateGroups="medical-secretaries" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="N_MS_DocumentsComplete" name="Are the documents complete now?" default="F7">
      <bpmn:documentation>Complete goes to clinical review; anything else asks the referring organisation again, which is the repeat of the request rather than an abandonment of it (BR-01, FR-003).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="N_MS_ReadyForReview" name="Referral ready for clinical review" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="N_MS_RequestDocuments" name="Request the missing information">
      <bpmn:documentation>Job type request-referral-documents (worker referral-document-request; publishes the message missing-information-requested to the referring organisation). Input: referralId, requestedFrom, requestedItems. Output: informationRequestStatus, informationRequestMessageKey. Error: INVALID_VARIABLE (FR-003, BR-02).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="request-referral-documents" retries="3" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="B_MS_ReceiptInvalid" name="receipt unusable" attachedToRef="N_MS_RecordReceipt">
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition errorRef="Error_INVALID_VARIABLE" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="B_MS_RequestInvalid" name="request unusable" attachedToRef="N_MS_RequestDocuments">
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition errorRef="Error_INVALID_VARIABLE" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F1" sourceRef="N_MS_ReferralReceived" targetRef="N_MS_MergeMissingItems" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F7" name="still incomplete" sourceRef="N_MS_DocumentsComplete" targetRef="N_MS_MergeMissingItems" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F8" sourceRef="B_MS_RequestInvalid" targetRef="N_MS_MergeMissingItems" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F10" sourceRef="B_MS_ReceiptInvalid" targetRef="N_MS_MergeMissingItems" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="MF1" sourceRef="N_MS_MergeMissingItems" targetRef="N_MS_RecordMissingItems" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F2" sourceRef="N_MS_RecordMissingItems" targetRef="N_MS_RequestDocuments" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F3" sourceRef="N_MS_RequestDocuments" targetRef="N_MS_DocumentsSupplied" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F4" sourceRef="N_MS_DocumentsSupplied" targetRef="N_MS_RecordReceipt" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F9" sourceRef="N_MS_RecordReceipt" targetRef="N_MS_CheckSuppliedDocuments" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F5" sourceRef="N_MS_CheckSuppliedDocuments" targetRef="N_MS_DocumentsComplete" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F6" name="complete" sourceRef="N_MS_DocumentsComplete" targetRef="N_MS_ReadyForReview">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">= documentsComplete = true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="Collaboration_1">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Participant_Hospital_di" bpmnElement="Participant_Hospital" isHorizontal="true">
